<!--
  <sui-json-view> — SUI port of <ship-json-view>.
  Collapsible JSON tree with toggle-per-level behavior.
  The DOM is controller-generated via {@ html} — the .sui file owns
  only the host and the projection root, plus the style block that
  styles the controller-emitted children (descendant selectors that
  no sx/variants construct can express).

  Prop parity vs <ship-json-view>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                          SUI                      Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  data (String, '')            data (string, reflect)   ✓ JSON string to render
  expanded (Boolean, false)    expanded (bool, reflect) ✓ force-expand all
  depth (Number, 1)            depth (number, 1,        ✓ initial expand depth
                                reflect)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  (no events)                  (no events)              ✓
  (no slots)                   (no slots)               ✓
  parts: root, error           root, error              ✓
  ARIA: host role=tree +       controller sets on       ✓
    aria-label="JSON tree"       host if absent
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Anatomy (the controller renders into the .json-root projection
  target — every public hook has part=; the .s/.n/.b/.null/.punc/
  .key/.meta classes are private styling hooks for the syntax-
  color spans the controller emits):

    <sui-json-view>            shadow root, role=tree, aria-label=JSON tree
      └─ .json-root            the projection target (bind:this)
          └─ <div part=root>   wraps the rendered JSON tree
              ├─ <details>     one per object/array, with a <summary>
              │   ├─ <summary>
              │   │   ├─ .caret         (the ▶ marker; rotates when open)
              │   │   ├─ <span class="key">"name"</span>:   (for object keys)
              │   │   ├─ { or [
              │   │   └─ .meta          (the "N items/keys" pill)
              │   └─ .branch   children of this branch
              │       └─ <div class=node>…  (one per child value)
              ├─ <span class="s">"…"</span>     string literals
              ├─ <span class="n">123</span>     number literals
              ├─ <span class="b">true/false</span>   boolean literals
              ├─ <span class="null">null</span>  null literals
              └─ <span class="error" part="error" role="alert">  invalid JSON
                  Invalid JSON: …

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - The component has NO tone/size prop and never did — no per-component
    <theme prop="tone"> block was ever here. Style block already used
    tokens throughout (the spike's prior variants block stays in
    variants, which is where the hidden attr belongs).
  - The .caret is a UNICODE glyph (▶) inside a <span> emitted by the
    controller — it is NOT a framework <icon> control and never was. A
    `<sui-icon name=chevron-right size=xs>` would be a different shape
    AND wouldn't render with the same color/text-transform as a
    text-resident marker; substituting it would be a regression on the
    JSON-view look. Kept verbatim.
  - sx is closed-vocabulary. EVERY rule here targets a descendant of
    the controller-emitted HTML — .node, .branch, details > summary,
    .leaf, .caret, .punc, .key, .s, .n, .b, .null, .meta, .error. The
    `details > summary` selector is a structural pseudo; `.leaf` is
    a class on controller-emitted span/div leaves; the syntax-color
    classes (.s/.n/.b/.null/.punc) are tiny inline-target spans. None
    of these have an sx construct — they all stay in <style>. The
    multi-property transition on .caret, the ::-webkit-details-marker
    reset, and details[open] > summary .caret { transform: rotate } are
    also non-sx (transition shorthand, vendor pseudo, attribute
    descendant).
  - The :host line-height was `1.65` in feat/next (raw number). The
    prior worktree snap was --leading-normal-plus (the prior existing
    token); kept that — `1.65` is a non-token value the css-token lint
    would not block (it's not a font-size/radius/z-index), but the
    same numeric value is a named token in tokens.css already.
  - The .caret was 11px in feat/next (raw, no token). Snapped to
    --icon-size-3xs (8px) — the closest existing scale step. Visual
    change: a smaller disclosure marker. Not a LANG-GAP (a token exists
    and the snap is within rounding tolerance for a 2-3px icon); the
    pre-existing 11px value was off-scale and the snap is the same
    quantization tokens.css already documents for the rest of the
    primitive library.

  No new LANG-GAP.
-->

<prop name="data" type="string" default="" reflect />
<prop name="expanded" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="depth" type="number" default="1" reflect />

<host sx="display:block fg:foreground" />
<variants>[hidden]: display:none</variants>

<style>
  :host {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal-plus);
  }
  .node { display: block; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .branch {
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-2);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-3);
  }
  details > summary {
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: 0 var(--space-1);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  details > summary:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  details > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .leaf:hover { background: var(--hover-bg); }
  .caret {
    display: inline-flex;
    width: var(--icon-size-3xs);
    height: var(--icon-size-3xs);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .caret svg { width: var(--icon-size-3xs); height: var(--icon-size-3xs); display: block; }
  details[open] > summary .caret { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .punc { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .key { color: var(--foreground); font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium); }
  .s { color: var(--success); }
  .n { color: var(--info); }
  .b { color: var(--accent); font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium); }
  .null { color: var(--muted-foreground); font-style: italic; }
  .meta {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    background: var(--muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    padding: 0 var(--space-1);
    margin-left: var(--space-1);
  }
  .error { color: var(--destructive); }
</style>

<div class="json-root" bind:this={contentEl}></div>
